**Movement to work - Skelmersdale JobCentre

**Project Overview

The Movement to Work project is a two-week work-experience programme designed to help Jobcentre customers become more confident, develop employability skills and prepare for future work opportunities. 
The programme will be delivered through Skelmersdale Jobcentre and will run for approximately six days across two weeks. Participants will attend from Monday to Wednesday, usually between 10:00am and 3:00pm.
The programme will combine practical work experience with employability support. Participants will learn about different roles within the Jobcentre, complete workplace activities and receive guidance on applying for jobs.

**The programme will cover:

*CV creation and improvement
*Cover-letter writing
*Personal-statement writing
*Job-application skills
*Interview preparation
*Appropriate and effective use of artificial intelligence
*Communication skills
*Teamwork
*Time management
*Technical and digital skills
*Social and interpersonal skills
*Understanding different Jobcentre roles
*Supporting outreach to encourage eligible customers to join the programme
*Learning about local employment sectors and opportunities
*Understanding travel options for local work opportunities

Participants will receive one-to-one support throughout the programme and will be awarded a certificate of participation that can be added to their CV.
The supporting website will clearly explain what Movement to Work is, what participants will do, the benefits of joining and how the programme can help them move closer to employment.
